  "notes": "Modified cash basis city, treated as cash basis. Governmental lines, transfers and bond/loan proceeds from the governmental funds statement (p5-6, Total Governmental Funds column); beginning/ending cash = beginning/ending total fund balances (fund balances are cash plus LB 840 loans receivable 202,870, no liabilities). 'Property and motor vehicle' 1,033,141 split by the tax labels the fund schedules print: General 736,361 'Property' (p14) and Debt Service 136,141 'Property taxes' (p17) as property tax; Street 160,639 'Property and motor vehicle taxes' stays unlabeled. Business-type (Light, Water, Sewer, Landfill) from the modified cash basis proprietary statement (p8-9, Total column): nonoperating capital outlay, principal and interest are disbursements, bond proceeds 1,300,583 in business_type.debt_proceeds, transfers out (370,205). Internal Service Fund (health insurance, net position 224,302) is excluded from both groups (not in the governmental funds statement; it is in the government-wide governmental column). The supplementary accrual-type proprietary statement (p10-11, with depreciation, net position 9,927,842) and cash flows (p12-13) are not recorded. Balance sheet: government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1) because its governmental column (7,517,917, includes the internal service fund) differs from the governmental funds balance sheet (7,293,615); component unit excluded; no liabilities printed. Detail: General Fund (p14-15), Street (p16) and Debt Service (p17) budget schedules; the All Funds budget schedule (p18-19) is combined, not per fund, and is not recorded to avoid double counting; Sales Tax, Economic Development, Keno and utility funds have no own schedule; component unit schedule (p20) skipped. Street Fund 'Charges for services' has a budget only (1,000), no actual, not recorded. Read pages 1-20 of 20."
